seClass, the \"tumour suppressor gene\" wording is a gene class rather than a disease, and the bare \"disease\" references are general terms, so none of those are annotated.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"decisions\":[{\"id\":1,\"entity\":\"CompositeMention\",\"rationale\":\"\\\"breast/ovarian\\\" is a contiguous string referring to two separate diseases (breast cancer and ovarian cancer) joined by a slash, analogous to the guideline's composite example, and it is used adjectivally for 'family'.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Annotation Guidelines 2 (Composite Mention) and 3 (Modifier)\"},{\"id\":2,\"entity\":\"CompositeMention\",\"rationale\":\"\\\"breast / ovarian cancer\\\" contiguously refers to two separate diseases (breast cancer and ovarian cancer) sharing the head term 'cancer', so it is one Composite Mention, used as a modifier of 'pedigree'.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Annotation Guidelines 2 (Composite Mention) and 3 (Modifier)\"},{\"id\":3,\"entity\":\"NONE\",\"rationale\":\"\\\"disease\\\" is a very general term used only to say the family is affected by the disease, with no specific disease name, so it is excluded.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What NOT to Annotate 4 (general terms)\"},{\"id\":4,\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"\\\"breast cancer\\\" is a disease name used as a modifier of the noun 'case' in 'bilateral breast cancer case', so it is annotated as a Modifier.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Annotation Guidelines 3 (Modifier)\"},{\"id\":5,\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"\\\"breast tumour\\\" refers to a breast cancer disease mention and modifies the noun 'pairs' in 'breast tumour / blood pairs'; 'tumour' is retained as a disease term.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Annotation Guidelines 3 (Modifier); What NOT to Annotate 4 (tumor terms retained)\"},{\"id\":6,\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"\\\"tumours\\\" used alone refers to tumours in general (a family of tumour diseases) rather than one specific disease with a single definition; 'tumour' is retained as a disease term, so it is annotated as a Disease Class.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Annotation Guidelines 1 (Disease Class); What NOT to Annotate 4 (tumor terms retained)\"},{\"id\":7,\"entity\":\"NONE\",\"rationale\":\"In \\\"tumour suppressor gene\\\" the word 'tumour' names a class of genes, not a disease mention, so it should not be annotated.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What NOT to Annotate 4 (general terms) and 5 (non-disease biological concepts)\"},{\"id\":8,\"entity\":\"NONE\",\"rationale\":\"\\\"disease\\\" in \\\"disease-bearing chromosome\\\" is a very general term that does not name a specific disease, so it is excluded.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What NOT to Annotate 4 (general terms)\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4363, "output_tokens": 4252, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 3288}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}